---
/**
 * "Bot-tan's Memory" — the wireframe space at /memory.
 *
 * Deliberately English-only and deliberately off-brand: the rest of the site is
 * a cream sketchbook, and this page is the inside of Bot-tan's head. It scopes
 * its own dark tokens rather than touching `global.css`, which every other page
 * shares.
 *
 * Everything drawn here comes from the public `/memory-graph` endpoint, which
 * publishes impression labels and their aggregates and nothing else — no
 * conversation text, no links back to anyone's posts.
 */
import {
  EDGE_COLOR,
  GRID_COLOR,
  HIGHLIGHT,
  KIND_COLORS,
  PANEL,
  SURFACE,
  TEXT_PRIMARY,
  TEXT_SECONDARY,
} from '../../lib/memoryTheme';
---

<section
  class="memory"
  style={`--mem-surface:${SURFACE};--mem-panel:${PANEL};--mem-text:${TEXT_PRIMARY};--mem-text-soft:${TEXT_SECONDARY};--mem-grid:${GRID_COLOR};--mem-work:${KIND_COLORS.work};--mem-word:${KIND_COLORS.word};--mem-edge:${EDGE_COLOR};--mem-highlight:${HIGHLIGHT};`}
>
  <header class="memory__head">
    <p class="memory__eyebrow">bot-tan / memory</p>
    <h1 class="memory__title">Bot-tan's Memory</h1>
    <p class="memory__lead">
      Every conversation Bot-tan has leaves a few words behind. This is what stuck: the
      things she found memorable, how strongly, how recently, and which of them she
      thinks belong together.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="memory__hud" role="status">
    <div class="memory__hud-cell">
      <span class="memory__hud-key">link</span>
      <span class="memory__hud-value" id="mem-link">connecting…</span>
    </div>
    <div class="memory__hud-cell">
      <span class="memory__hud-key">state</span>
      <span class="memory__hud-value" id="mem-state">—</span>
    </div>
    <div class="memory__hud-cell memory__hud-cell--wide">
      <span class="memory__hud-key">doing</span>
      <span class="memory__hud-value" id="mem-mood">—</span>
    </div>
    <div class="memory__hud-cell">
      <span class="memory__hud-key">nodes</span>
      <span class="memory__hud-value" id="mem-nodes">—</span>
    </div>
    <div class="memory__hud-cell">
      <span class="memory__hud-key">links</span>
      <span class="memory__hud-value" id="mem-edges">—</span>
    </div>
    <div class="memory__hud-cell">
      <span class="memory__hud-key">synced</span>
      <span class="memory__hud-value" id="mem-synced">—</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="memory__controls">
    <label class="memory__search">
      <span class="memory__search-label">filter</span>
      <input
        type="search"
        id="mem-search"
        placeholder="type a word…"
        autocomplete="off"
        spellcheck="false"
      />
    </label>

    <div class="memory__views" role="group" aria-label="View">
      <button type="button" id="mem-view-graph" class="memory__view is-active" aria-pressed="true">
        graph
      </button>
      <button type="button" id="mem-view-list" class="memory__view" aria-pressed="false">
        list
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="memory__stage">
    <div class="memory__canvas-wrap" id="mem-graph-view">
      <canvas id="mem-canvas" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
      <p class="memory__empty" id="mem-empty" hidden>
        Nothing to show yet — either Bot-tan has not remembered enough, or her memory
        server is unreachable. The list view has the same data.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!--
      The canvas is invisible to assistive tech, so the same rows exist as real
      markup. It is a view toggle rather than a hidden fallback: reading the
      numbers is often what you actually came here to do.
    -->
    <div class="memory__list" id="mem-list-view" hidden>
      <table class="memory__table">
        <caption class="memory__table-caption">
          Ordered the way Bot-tan ranks a memory: impression first, then how
          recently and how often it came up.
        </caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">word</th>
            <th scope="col">kind</th>
            <th scope="col">impression</th>
            <th scope="col">times</th>
            <th scope="col">last seen</th>
            <th scope="col">connected to</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody id="mem-list-body"></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <aside class="memory__readout" id="mem-readout" aria-live="polite">
      <p class="memory__readout-hint">
        Point at a node — or pick a row in the list — to read what Bot-tan knows about it.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </div>

  <div class="memory__legend">
    <h2 class="memory__legend-title">Legend</h2>
    <ul class="memory__legend-list">
      <li><span class="memory__swatch memory__swatch--work" aria-hidden="true"></span> a work — a game, a show, a book</li>
      <li><span class="memory__swatch memory__swatch--word" aria-hidden="true"></span> a word — anything else worth keeping</li>
      <li><span class="memory__swatch memory__swatch--size" aria-hidden="true"></span> bigger = stronger impression</li>
      <li><span class="memory__swatch memory__swatch--dashed-ring" aria-hidden="true"></span> dashed outline = not scored yet</li>
      <li><span class="memory__swatch memory__swatch--fade" aria-hidden="true"></span> brighter = remembered more recently</li>
      <li><span class="memory__swatch memory__swatch--solid" aria-hidden="true"></span> solid line = came up in the same conversation</li>
      <li><span class="memory__swatch memory__swatch--dashed" aria-hidden="true"></span> dashed line = close in meaning (embedding vectors)</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <p class="memory__note">
    Only public conversations are here, and only the words themselves — never what
    anyone said, who said it, or a link back to it. Things she was told in confidence
    are remembered, but they never reach this page. The graph refreshes on its own
    every minute; the server rebuilds it every ten.
  </p>
</section>

<script>
  import { connectBotStatus, type BotStatusPayload, type ConnectionState } from '../../lib/botStatus';
  import { fetchMemoryGraph, EMPTY_MEMORY_GRAPH, type MemoryGraph, type MemoryNode } from '../../lib/botMemoryGraph';
  import { createMemoryGraphView, type MemoryGraphView } from '../../lib/memoryGraphCanvas';

  const POLL_MS = 60_000;

  const canvas = document.getElementById('mem-canvas') as HTMLCanvasElement | null;
  const search = document.getElementById('mem-search') as HTMLInputElement | null;
  const listBody = document.getElementById('mem-list-body');
  const listView = document.getElementById('mem-list-view');
  const graphView = document.getElementById('mem-graph-view');
  const readout = document.getElementById('mem-readout');
  const empty = document.getElementById('mem-empty');
  const graphButton = document.getElementById('mem-view-graph');
  const listButton = document.getElementById('mem-view-list');

  const hud = {
    link: document.getElementById('mem-link'),
    state: document.getElementById('mem-state'),
    mood: document.getElementById('mem-mood'),
    nodes: document.getElementById('mem-nodes'),
    edges: document.getElementById('mem-edges'),
    synced: document.getElementById('mem-synced'),
  };

  if (canvas) {
    const reducedMotion = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
    let graph: MemoryGraph = EMPTY_MEMORY_GRAPH;
    let view: MemoryGraphView | null = null;
    let pollTimer: ReturnType<typeof setInterval> | undefined;

    const relative = (iso: string): string => {
      const at = Date.parse(iso);
      if (!Number.isFinite(at)) return '—';
      const days = Math.floor((Date.now() - at) / 86_400_000);
      if (days <= 0) return 'today';
      if (days === 1) return 'yesterday';
      if (days < 30) return `${days} days ago`;
      const months = Math.round(days / 30);
      return months < 12 ? `${months} months ago` : `${Math.round(days / 365)} years ago`;
    };

    const neighboursOf = (id: string): string[] => {
      const found: string[] = [];
      for (const edge of graph.edges) {
        if (edge.source === id) found.push(edge.target);
        else if (edge.target === id) found.push(edge.source);
      }
      return found;
    };

    const labelOf = (id: string) => graph.nodes.find((node) => node.id === id)?.label ?? id;

    function renderReadout(node: MemoryNode | null) {
      if (!readout) return;
      if (!node) {
        readout.innerHTML =
          '<p class="memory__readout-hint">Point at a node — or pick a row in the list — to read what Bot-tan knows about it.</p>';
        return;
      }
      const linked = neighboursOf(node.id).map(labelOf);
      const impression =
        node.salience === null
          ? 'not scored yet'
          : `${node.salience} / 100${node.scoredCount > 0 ? ` (from ${node.scoredCount} scored)` : ''}`;

      readout.innerHTML = `
        <p class="memory__readout-label">${escapeHtml(node.label)}</p>
        ${node.spokenForm ? `<p class="memory__readout-spoken">she says it &ldquo;${escapeHtml(node.spokenForm)}&rdquo;</p>` : ''}
        <dl class="memory__readout-rows">
          <dt>kind</dt><dd>${node.kind === 'work' ? 'a work' : 'a word'}</dd>
          <dt>impression</dt><dd>${escapeHtml(impression)}</dd>
          <dt>came up</dt><dd>${node.occurrences} times</dd>
          <dt>last seen</dt><dd>${escapeHtml(relative(node.latestAt))}</dd>
        </dl>
        ${linked.length > 0 ? `<p class="memory__readout-linked"><span>connected to</span> ${linked.map((l) => `<em>${escapeHtml(l)}</em>`).join(', ')}</p>` : ''}
      `;
    }

    function escapeHtml(value: string): string {
      const div = document.createElement('div');
      div.textContent = value;
      return div.innerHTML;
    }

    function renderList() {
      if (!listBody) return;
      listBody.textContent = '';
      for (const node of graph.nodes) {
        const row = document.createElement('tr');
        row.tabIndex = 0;
        row.dataset.id = node.id;
        const cells = [
          node.spokenForm ? `${node.label} (${node.spokenForm})` : node.label,
          node.kind === 'work' ? 'work' : 'word',
          node.salience === null ? 'not scored' : String(node.salience),
          String(node.occurrences),
          relative(node.latestAt),
          neighboursOf(node.id).map(labelOf).join(', ') || '—',
        ];
        for (const value of cells) {
          const cell = document.createElement('td');
          cell.textContent = value;
          row.append(cell);
        }
        const focusRow = () => {
          view?.select(node.id);
          renderReadout(node);
        };
        row.addEventListener('focus', focusRow);
        row.addEventListener('mouseenter', focusRow);
        listBody.append(row);
      }
    }

    function renderHud() {
      if (hud.nodes) hud.nodes.textContent = String(graph.nodes.length);
      if (hud.edges) {
        const similar = graph.edges.filter((edge) => edge.type === 'similarity').length;
        hud.edges.textContent = graph.similarityAvailable
          ? `${graph.edges.length} (${similar} by meaning)`
          : `${graph.edges.length} (co-occurrence only)`;
      }
      if (hud.synced) {
        hud.synced.textContent = graph.generatedAt
          ? new Date(graph.generatedAt).toLocaleTimeString(undefined, {
              hour: '2-digit',
              minute: '2-digit',
            })
          : '—';
      }
      if (empty) empty.hidden = graph.nodes.length > 0;
    }

    async function refresh() {
      const next = await fetchMemoryGraph();
      // A failed poll must not wipe a graph that is already on screen.
      if (next.nodes.length === 0 && graph.nodes.length > 0) return;
      graph = next;
      view?.update(graph);
      renderList();
      renderHud();
    }

    async function boot() {
      view = await createMemoryGraphView({
        canvas: canvas!,
        onSelect: renderReadout,
        reducedMotion,
      });
      await refresh();
      startPolling();
    }

    function startPolling() {
      stopPolling();
      pollTimer = setInterval(() => void refresh(), POLL_MS);
    }

    function stopPolling() {
      if (pollTimer !== undefined) clearInterval(pollTimer);
      pollTimer = undefined;
    }

    // Nothing here is worth a request or a repaint while the tab is hidden.
    document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', () => {
      if (document.hidden) stopPolling();
      else {
        void refresh();
        startPolling();
      }
    });

    search?.addEventListener('input', () => {
      view?.setFilter(search.value);
    });

    function showView(which: 'graph' | 'list') {
      const isGraph = which === 'graph';
      if (graphView) graphView.hidden = !isGraph;
      if (listView) listView.hidden = isGraph;
      graphButton?.classList.toggle('is-active', isGraph);
      listButton?.classList.toggle('is-active', !isGraph);
      graphButton?.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(isGraph));
      listButton?.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(!isGraph));
      // The canvas was display:none, so it has no box to measure until now.
      if (isGraph) view?.resize();
    }

    graphButton?.addEventListener('click', () => showView('graph'));
    listButton?.addEventListener('click', () => showView('list'));

    // The physics bundle only loads once the space is actually on screen.
    const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries, self) => {
      for (const entry of entries) {
        if (!entry.isIntersecting) continue;
        self.disconnect();
        void boot();
      }
    }, { rootMargin: '160px' });
    observer.observe(canvas);

    // The live status line is the same socket the dashboard uses.
    const stateWords: Record<ConnectionState, string> = {
      connecting: 'connecting…',
      open: 'live',
      closed: 'offline',
      error: 'offline',
    };
    connectBotStatus({
      onStateChange: (state) => {
        if (hud.link) hud.link.textContent = stateWords[state];
      },
      onMessage: (payload: BotStatusPayload) => {
        if (hud.state) {
          hud.state.textContent = payload.status
            ? `${payload.status}${typeof payload.energy === 'number' ? ` · ${payload.energy}%` : ''}`
            : '—';
        }
        if (hud.mood) hud.mood.textContent = payload.mood_en || payload.mood || '—';
      },
    });
  }
</script>

<style>
  /*
   * Every token below is scoped to `.memory`. The site's own light tokens stay
   * untouched — the header and footer above and below this section keep looking
   * like themselves.
   */
  .memory {
    --mem-radius: 0.4rem;
    position: relative;
    margin: -1px 0 0;
    padding: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem) clamp(1rem, 4vw, 2.5rem) 3rem;
    background:
      radial-gradient(120% 80% at 50% 0%, #101d2c 0%, var(--mem-surface) 62%),
      var(--mem-surface);
    color: var(--mem-text);
    font-family: var(--font-dot), monospace;
    min-height: 100vh;
  }

  .memory::before {
    /* Faint scanlines. Purely atmosphere, so it never eats a pointer event. */
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
    background: repeating-linear-gradient(
      to bottom,
      rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.022) 0 1px,
      transparent 1px 3px
    );
  }

  .memory > * {
    position: relative;
    max-width: 72rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .memory__eyebrow {
    margin: 0;
    letter-spacing: 0.28em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--mem-work);
  }

  .memory__title {
    margin: 0.4rem 0 0.8rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 5vw, 2.8rem);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .memory__lead {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 44rem;
    line-height: 1.9;
    color: var(--mem-text-soft);
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .memory__hud {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(9rem, 1fr));
    gap: 1px;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--mem-edge) 40%, transparent);
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--mem-edge) 55%, transparent);
    border-radius: var(--mem-radius);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .memory__hud-cell {
    background: var(--mem-panel);
    padding: 0.6rem 0.8rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.2rem;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .memory__hud-cell--wide {
    grid-column: span 2;
  }

  .memory__hud-key {
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--mem-text-soft) 80%, transparent);
  }

  .memory__hud-value {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--mem-text);
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .memory__controls {
    margin-top: 1.2rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
  }

  .memory__search {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    flex: 1 1 16rem;
  }

  .memory__search-label {
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--mem-text-soft);
  }

  .memory__search input {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 0;
    background: var(--mem-panel);
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--mem-edge) 65%, transparent);
    border-radius: var(--mem-radius);
    padding: 0.5rem 0.7rem;
    color: var(--mem-text);
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .memory__search input:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--mem-highlight);
    outline-offset: 1px;
  }

  .memory__views {
    display: flex;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--mem-edge) 65%, transparent);
    border-radius: var(--mem-radius);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .memory__view {
    appearance: none;
    border: 0;
    background: var(--mem-panel);
    color: var(--mem-text-soft);
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .memory__view.is-active {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--mem-work) 30%, var(--mem-panel));
    color: var(--mem-text);
  }

  .memory__view:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--mem-highlight);
    outline-offset: -2px;
  }

  .memory__stage {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 17rem;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .memory__canvas-wrap,
  .memory__list {
    grid-column: 1;
    grid-row: 1;
    position: relative;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--mem-edge) 55%, transparent);
    border-radius: var(--mem-radius);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--mem-panel) 55%, transparent);
    min-height: 26rem;
  }

  .memory__canvas-wrap {
    height: min(70vh, 40rem);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  #mem-canvas {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    touch-action: pan-y;
  }

  .memory__empty {
    position: absolute;
    inset: auto 2rem 2rem;
    margin: 0;
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--mem-text-soft);
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .memory__list {
    max-height: min(70vh, 40rem);
    overflow: auto;
    padding: 0.5rem;
  }

  .memory__table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
  }

  .memory__table-caption {
    caption-side: top;
    text-align: left;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.5rem 0.8rem;
    color: var(--mem-text-soft);
    font-family: var(--font-body);
  }

  .memory__table th,
  .memory__table td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 0.45rem 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--mem-edge) 32%, transparent);
    vertical-align: top;
  }

  .memory__table th {
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
    background: var(--mem-panel);
    color: var(--mem-text-soft);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: 0.65rem;
  }

  .memory__table tbody tr:hover,
  .memory__table tbody tr:focus-visible {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--mem-highlight) 12%, transparent);
    outline: none;
  }

  .memory__table td:last-child {
    color: var(--mem-text-soft);
    max-width: 16rem;
  }

  .memory__readout {
    grid-column: 2;
    grid-row: 1;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--mem-edge) 55%, transparent);
    border-radius: var(--mem-radius);
    background: var(--mem-panel);
    padding: 1rem;
    min-height: 12rem;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  .memory__readout-hint {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--mem-text-soft);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .memory__readout :global(.memory__readout-label) {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-dot), monospace;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--mem-text);
    word-break: break-word;
  }

  .memory__readout :global(.memory__readout-spoken) {
    margin: 0.2rem 0 0;
    color: var(--mem-word);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }

  .memory__readout :global(.memory__readout-rows) {
    margin: 0.9rem 0 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
    gap: 0.35rem 0.8rem;
  }

  .memory__readout :global(.memory__readout-rows dt) {
    color: var(--mem-text-soft);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    align-self: center;
  }

  .memory__readout :global(.memory__readout-rows dd) {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--mem-text);
  }

  .memory__readout :global(.memory__readout-linked) {
    margin: 0.9rem 0 0;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--mem-text);
  }

  .memory__readout :global(.memory__readout-linked span) {
    display: block;
    color: var(--mem-text-soft);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .memory__readout :global(.memory__readout-linked em) {
    font-style: normal;
    color: var(--mem-highlight);
  }

  .memory__legend {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .memory__legend-title {
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--mem-text-soft);
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .memory__legend-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(15rem, 1fr));
    gap: 0.5rem 1.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--mem-text-soft);
  }

  .memory__legend-list li {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.6rem;
  }

  .memory__swatch {
    flex: none;
    width: 1.4rem;
    height: 1rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .memory__swatch--work::before,
  .memory__swatch--word::before,
  .memory__swatch--size::before,
  .memory__swatch--dashed-ring::before,
  .memory__swatch--fade::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0 auto 0 0;
